The 3D menu's per-file entries for a local file are the stereo layer's menu, "3D Input Format", and its choices are
kept in the layer's per-file store, the one Dolphin and the thumbnailers read (ORDER 551; Daniel, 2026-10-07: "Each
viewer keeps only its view adapter and its 3D menu"; 2026-10-23: "never touch the user file"). A picture set to Not 3D
or given a packing in Dolphin opens that way here, the menu shows what the store holds, and a choice made here shows
in Dolphin. The input packing and Not 3D, which were this session's, are now the file's.

Nothing Gwenview offered is gone: the layer's menu holds Automatic, Not 3D, side by side and top and bottom in
either order, the anaglyph pairs and the swap, and adds the interleaved packings, picture and depth and Save the
correction into the file. Stereo, Left eye only and Right eye only stay in the 3D menu as this session's view. The
shortcuts of the entries the layer's menu replaces (Alt+Shift+A, S, R, T, B, W, C and N) keep working and act on the
same store. A file that is not local has no place in the store and keeps the session's input and its swap in
gwenviewstereorc, as before, by those shortcuts.

The swaps Gwenview kept for local files in gwenviewstereorc are taken into the store once, at the first start, the
files untouched; a file that already has a choice in the store keeps it. Afterwards those entries are not read
again. When the store cannot be written the person is told and the next start tries again.

A file's choice follows it when it is renamed or moved (Stereo::FileChoiceMoves).

The picture area is opaque around the picture: the window's hole is the rectangle where the stereo picture shows,
the view's own background around it (ORDER 504, staged as +stereo3d9 and never published; this version carries it).

Built against libstereo-layer-dev 1.18.0.
